WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.557 --> 00:00:15.844
The afternoon before Pollyanna's arrival, Miss Polly inspected the attic room.

2
00:00:18.125 --> 00:00:21.026
A fly buzzed at one of the closed windows, trying to escape.

3
00:00:23.007 --> 00:00:26.849
Miss Polly killed the fly, opened the window, and swept the fly outside.

4
00:00:28.911 --> 00:00:31.212
Then she went downstairs and stood at the kitchen door.

5
00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:33.981
"Nancy," Miss Polly said.

6
00:00:34.001 --> 00:00:37.484
"I found a fly in Miss Pollyanna's room.

7
00:00:38.644 --> 00:00:41.546
Until the new screens come, keep the windows closed."

8
00:00:43.087 --> 00:00:44.128
Nancy stopped ironing.

9
00:00:44.148 --> 00:00:45.369
"Yes, ma'am."

10
00:00:45.389 --> 00:00:51.473
"My niece will arrive tomorrow afternoon at four o'clock," Miss Polly went on.

11
00:00:51.493 --> 00:00:54.435
"Tom will drive you to the station to meet her.

12
00:00:55.316 --> 00:00:59.639
The telegram said, 'blond hair, red gingham dress, straw hat.'

13
00:01:00.599 --> 00:01:03.998
That's all I know, but that's enough information for you to find her."

14
00:01:04.018 --> 00:01:07.320
"Yes, ma'am," Nancy said again.

15
00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:11.682
"But shouldn't you—" "No, I don't need to go."

16
00:01:12.563 --> 00:01:13.604
Miss Polly walked away.

17
00:01:14.844 --> 00:01:15.925
Nancy picked up her iron.

18
00:01:15.945 --> 00:01:21.189
"Blond hair, red gingham dress, straw hat.

19
00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:26.212
I'd be ashamed to admit that's all I know about my only niece."

20
00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:31.962
The next afternoon Tom drove Nancy to the station.

21
00:01:33.302 --> 00:01:36.064
As the train whistle sounded, Nancy was suddenly nervous.

22
00:01:37.325 --> 00:01:41.047
But she soon spotted a girl with two blond braids in a red gingham dress.

23
00:01:42.347 --> 00:01:46.330
Beneath a straw hat, an eager freckled face looked all around.

24
00:01:47.730 --> 00:01:49.031
Nancy approached the child.

25
00:01:49.051 --> 00:01:52.273
"Are you Miss Pollyanna?"

26
00:01:52.293 --> 00:01:57.276
"Yes!" The next moment Pollyanna was hugging Nancy tightly.

27
00:01:58.452 --> 00:02:00.893
"I'm so glad, glad, glad to see you!

28
00:02:00.913 --> 00:02:05.095
Of course I'm Pollyanna, and I hoped you'd come to meet me."

29
00:02:05.115 --> 00:02:06.755
"You did?"

30
00:02:07.936 --> 00:02:10.977
Nancy couldn't understand how Pollyanna knew she'd be at the station.

31
00:02:10.997 --> 00:02:13.998
"I've been wondering what you looked like."

32
00:02:15.199 --> 00:02:16.759
Pollyanna danced around Nancy.

33
00:02:16.779 --> 00:02:20.821
"I'm glad you look just like you do."

34
00:02:23.082 --> 00:02:24.743
Nancy didn't know how to reply.

35
00:02:26.023 --> 00:02:29.757
She was relieved when Tom walked over and offered to find Pollyanna's trunk.

36
00:02:33.839 --> 00:02:38.362
a brand-new trunk," Pollyanna explained as Nancy guided her toward the wagon.

37
00:02:38.382 --> 00:02:45.406
"The Ladies' Aid—the women's group at Father's church—was saving money for a new church carpet.

38
00:02:46.026 --> 00:02:48.168
But the ladies bought me a trunk instead.

39
00:02:49.268 --> 00:02:53.011
Anyway, the Ladies' Aiders—do you have Ladies' Aiders at your church?

40
00:02:53.711 --> 00:02:55.172
Father said many churches do.

41
00:02:56.032 --> 00:02:58.353
They helped Father bring me up after Mother died."

42
00:02:59.833 --> 00:03:02.394
Pollyanna kept up a stream of comments and questions.

43
00:03:03.654 --> 00:03:07.515
By the time Tom returned with the trunk, Nancy was dazed and breathless.

44
00:03:08.816 --> 00:03:11.136
But Pollyanna was still full of energy.

45
00:03:11.577 --> 00:03:13.277
She climbed up and sat between them.

46
00:03:13.297 --> 00:03:15.518
"This is lovely!"

47
00:03:15.818 --> 00:03:17.918
Pollyanna said as they started on their way.

48
00:03:17.938 --> 00:03:20.239
"Is it far to your house?

49
00:03:21.179 --> 00:03:23.180
I hope it is because I love to ride.

50
00:03:23.948 --> 00:03:26.289
But if it isn't, I'll be glad to get there soon.

51
00:03:31.611 --> 00:03:33.252
What a pretty town!

52
00:03:33.872 --> 00:03:35.513
I knew this town would be pretty.

53
00:03:36.033 --> 00:03:42.696
Father told me he remembered—" Pollyanna stopped, and Nancy noticed her eyes filling with tears.

54
00:03:43.957 --> 00:03:46.038
But in a moment, the little girl hurried on.

55
00:03:46.058 --> 00:03:52.148
"I suppose you wonder why I'm wearing red instead of black for mourning.

56
00:03:52.168 --> 00:03:55.070
There wasn't anything black in the donation box at church.

57
00:03:56.271 --> 00:03:57.913
Do you have donation boxes here?

58
00:03:58.933 --> 00:04:01.835
They're full of clothes and things that people don't want anymore.

59
00:04:02.856 --> 00:04:04.898
But they think poor people will want them."

60
00:04:04.918 --> 00:04:09.361
"I'm sure your dress will be fine," Nancy said.

61
00:04:09.381 --> 00:04:12.984
"It would be harder to be glad in black."

62
00:04:14.225 --> 00:04:16.246
"Glad?" Nancy said in surprise.

63
00:04:16.266 --> 00:04:22.130
"Yes, glad that Father has gone to heaven to be with Mother and their babies.

64
00:04:23.291 --> 00:04:28.293
He said I must be glad, which was awfully hard when I just had the Ladies' Aid.

65
00:04:29.234 --> 00:04:32.776
But now I've got you, Aunt Polly, and I'm so glad!"

66
00:04:34.217 --> 00:04:37.318
Nancy's eyes widened as she realized Pollyanna's mistake.

67
00:04:37.338 --> 00:04:39.720
"I'm not your aunt Polly.

68
00:04:39.740 --> 00:04:42.781
I'm only Nancy, a girl who works for her!"

69
00:04:42.801 --> 00:04:46.443
"Oh," Pollyanna said anxiously.

70
00:04:47.736 --> 00:04:49.737
"But there is an Aunt Polly, right?"

71
00:04:51.859 --> 00:04:52.599
Tom chuckled.

72
00:04:52.619 --> 00:04:55.661
"There sure is."

73
00:04:57.002 --> 00:04:58.103
Pollyanna relaxed.

74
00:04:58.123 --> 00:05:03.247
"Then I'm glad I can look forward to meeting her.

75
00:05:04.647 --> 00:05:06.229
Is Aunt Polly rich, Nancy?"

76
00:05:07.730 --> 00:05:08.370
"Yes, miss."

77
00:05:09.691 --> 00:05:13.173
"I hope she has carpets and pictures in every room.

78
00:05:14.154 --> 00:05:17.016
I love pictures, but we didn't have any.

79
00:05:18.028 --> 00:05:19.969
Father found one in the donation box.

80
00:05:21.010 --> 00:05:23.771
It was so nice that he sold it to buy me shoes.

81
00:05:26.293 --> 00:05:28.094
What a beautiful house!"

82
00:05:29.134 --> 00:05:31.476
Pollyanna exclaimed as they came up the drive.

83
00:05:33.277 --> 00:05:38.300
Nancy thought about the plain attic room and silently vowed to stay at Miss Polly's house forever.

84
00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:42.342
"This poor child needs someone to love her!"
